lar matrix\n- **III.** $det(R)=\\frac{4}{5} - \\sqrt{2}$\n\n$$\nR=\\begin{bmatrix}- \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & \\frac{2}{5} & - \\sqrt{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & \\frac{4}{5} & \\frac{3 \\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ - \\frac{3 \\sqrt{2}}{4} & \\frac{2}{5} & - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" 13194139535798 17592186045443 true] [17592186529214 1072 #uuid "2eb19151-d434-5c12-a703-9c37eed13782" 13194139535798 17592186045443 true] [17592186529214 1074 "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(R) & =|\\begin{aligned}- \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & \\frac{2}{5} & - \\sqrt{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & \\frac{4}{5} & \\frac{3 \\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ - \\frac{3 \\sqrt{2}}{4} & \\frac{2}{5} & - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(- \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{5} & \\frac{3 \\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ \\frac{2}{5} & - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}|+(- \\frac{2}{5})|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & \\frac{3 \\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ - \\frac{3 \\sqrt{2}}{4} & - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}|+(- \\sqrt{2})|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & \\frac{4}{5} \\\\ - \\frac{3 \\sqrt{2}}{4} & \\frac{2}{5}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(- \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})(- \\frac{2 \\sqrt{2}}{5}- \\frac{3 \\sqrt{2}}{5})+(- \\frac{2}{5})(- \\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{9}{4})+(- \\sqrt{2})(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{5}+\\frac{3 \\sqrt{2}}{5}) \\\\  & =(- \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})\\cdot (- \\sqrt{2})+(- \\frac{2}{5})\\cdot \\frac{7}{4}+(- \\sqrt{2})\\cdot \\frac{4 \\sqrt{2}}{5} \\\\  & =1- \\frac{7}{10}- \\frac{8}{5} \\\\  & =- \\frac{13}{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(R)=- \\frac{13}{10}\\ne 0$, the matrix is **not** singular. \n\nTherefore, only statement II is true." 13194139535798 17592186045443 true] [17592186529215 1080 "false" 13194139535798 17592186045443 true] [17592186529215 1082 #edb/ref